   "title": "Shunt motor and power flow",
   "body": "In a **shunt** motor the field (with an adjustable $R_{adj}$) is in parallel with the armature on the same supply: $I_F = V_T/(R_F + R_{adj})$, $I_L = I_A + I_F$.\n- $P_{in} = V_TI_L$\n- field loss $V_TI_F$, armature copper loss $I_A^2R_A$\n- $P_{dev} = E_AI_A$, then rotational losses (friction, windage, core)\n- $P_{out} = T_{out}\\omega_m = P_{dev} - P_{rot}$",
