  {
   "title": "Starting current",
   "body": "At standstill $E_A = 0$, so only the small $R_A$ limits the current: $I_A = V_T/R_A$, often 10–20 times the rated current. A **starting resistor** in series with the armature limits it; it is cut out step by step as the speed, and with it $E_A$, builds up.",
   "formula": "I_{A,start} = \\frac{V_T}{R_A + R_{start}}"
  }
